A||||8||spike||v8 Fiero 12.64 @ 111mph 1/4 mile
Z||000000||spike||05-17-99||07:25 AM||||I went to the Napierville Dragway this week-end and say my first v8 Fiero in action. The car itself was nothing special to look at. I think it was an 84 base model. But, and I mean but, this thing flew. I did not get the chance to speek to the owner, but it looks like a small block engine. The only thing is the motor was mounted from front to back and not side to side like the v8-archie installation. He did not bother burning or heating up his tires at all. The car just stuck to the ground, well the back end at least. With ever lurch forward the front would lift off the ground. Imagine crusing down the main while pulling wheelies in your car, a definate attention getter. I MUST HAVE ONE.
Z||000001||Patrick||05-17-99||12:26 PM||||<br>PICTURES, WE WANT PICTURES  !!!!!!<p>Sorry...<p>I'd love to see how the heck a V8 could be crammed in there facing front to back. That would make for an interesting transmission and rear end configuration too.<p>
Z||000002||Pretender||05-17-99||02:40 PM||||in Carlise this weekend  i seen some guy had a corvette engine front to back like mentioned above, it looked like a better fit too..thats what i'd like to see, a front to back northstar.....(in my '88 that is)
Z||000003||theogre||05-17-99||03:09 PM||||the use of a cadilac eldorado transmission comes to mind as to how you pull this off. Those were inline motors, and front wheel drive. the axle passes under the engine. very strange setup.
Z||000004||spike||05-18-99||06:47 AM||||Sorry I was not able to get pictures nor talk to the owner. I am going to try to find out his name and contact him. I will try to go to Napierville again this week-end. I hope he will be back, because I have many questions to ask. Once I find out how he did it I will let everyone know.
Z||000005||Pretender||05-19-99||04:21 AM||||111mph is kinda low for a 12 second car, shouldn't it be faster?., this still confuses me even though i race almost every weekend.
Z||000006||LEE498||05-19-99||09:20 AM||||Those were my same thoughts!
Z||000007||LEE498||05-19-99||09:27 AM||||But it can be the gearing of the trans too!
Z||000008||spike||05-20-99||11:03 AM||||As far as I am concerned 111mph is fast enough for me. I owned a 87 Mustang GT and never really went beyond this speed. I guess that is why my friends called me a wimp. I like to pamper my car. D'ont get my wrong I do punch it at times, but I am always gentile. The most important thing for me is the get-up and go power. If my car ends up doing 12.64 at 111mph I will be a very happy camper and I can asure you that no one would put down the 111mph trap speed. For about 8000.00 cdn. this car would kick-butt and not be just another stang of camaro.<p>
